  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The mass of gas adsorbed,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>, per unit mass of adsorbate,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, was measured at various pressures,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>A&nbsp;graph between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>&nbsp;gives a straight line with slope equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and the intercept equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;at a pressure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atm</mi></math>&nbsp;is :</p><p>(Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4771</mn></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "48",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0071_484d518f7e0f.png\" style=\"width: 298px; height: 230px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi></math></p><p>Slope&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Intercept ,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>477</mn></math> So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>477</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>[</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo>]</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math></p>"
  }
